Journey: A claim's events arrive on Kafka in business order, keyed by claim, each matching the event contract
Id: claim-event-sequence
Tags: @kafka @integration @contract @regression
Role: adjuster
Risk: 4
Requirements: EVT-1, EVT-2, EVT-4

Start listening on Kafka topic "larkspur.claims.events" on events as stream
Run code "steps/claims.steps.ts#seedClaim" with policyId="POL-M-200455", type="COLLISION", amount="2210" as seeded
Set variable claimId to seeded.claimId

Log in
Open ${BACKOFFICE_URL}/claims/${claimId}
  Expect the page contains "Review claim ${claimId}"
Select "Partially covered" from @ClaimDesk.reason
Clear @ClaimDesk.approvedAmount
Type "1980" into @ClaimDesk.approvedAmount
Click @ClaimDesk.approve
  Expect the page contains "Claim ${claimId} approved"

Wait for 3 messages in stream where "$.claimId" = "${claimId}" within 20 s matching schema "schemas/claim-event.schema.json" as lifecycle
Expect join(pluck(lifecycle, "type"), ",") == "claim.submitted,claim.in_review,claim.approved"
Expect ${lifecycle_meta.0.key} equals "${claimId}"
Expect ${lifecycle.2.approvedAmount} == 1980
Expect ${lifecycle.2.payoutAmount} == 1230
Verify no messages arrive in stream where "$.claimId" = "${claimId}" and "$.type" = "claim.rejected" within 2 s
Stop listening to stream
Run code "steps/claims.steps.ts#removeClaim" with claimId="${claimId}" as cleanup
